{"id":"slice4-path-order-landmine","parent":"def-infra","ord":"a1","title":"Slice 4 must pick one path order #deferral","done":"2026-08-20T20:32:37-04:00","desc":"**Recorded by the slice-3 author (PR #211):** the patcher places an arriving file by assemble's plain string path compare, while the web client's `sortByPath` sorts segment by segment.\n- The two already disagree today — not new unsoundness.\n- But slice 4 (the browser folding delta frames through the same patcher) has to pick one ordering, or the patched browser view will disagree with the assembled one.\n- Filed on the human's overnight draft ruling (\"file roadmap entries for those three\").","created":"2026-08-16T23:15:14-04:00","changed":"2026-08-20T20:32:37-04:00","custom":{"from":"211","retired":"2026-08-20 verification vs master 44bc6873 — slice 4 landed a third exit: one comparator byPath in @olai/format (paths.ts:42) spent by assemble (set.ts:160), the patcher (patch.ts:291) and the client (web paths.ts:47); orderings pinned by set.test.ts:187,193; and the browser no longer folds through the patcher at all. Nothing left to decide."}}
{"id":"html-unreadable-refused-state","parent":"def-infra","ord":"a0","title":"An unreadable page says so on the page #deferral","todo":true,"desc":"#204's deferral 1.\n- Under load-on-read, an unreadable .html (permissions, vanished mid-read) reports only to the server log — the reader sees the page with no body.\n- Telling them needs a `\"refused\"` state on DocumentEntry (a wire change with its own argument) and a face for it.\n- Still quieter than what it replaced, which failed the whole probe and bannered the whole directory.","created":"2026-08-16T12:49:32-04:00","changed":"2026-08-20T20:28:46-04:00","custom":{"from":"204"}}
{"id":"patch-refile-fifth-spelling","parent":"def-infra","ord":"a2","title":"patch.ts spells re-file-a-reverse-index five times #techdebt #deferral","todo":true,"desc":"Counted at PR #237 by the reuse pass.\n\n- **Pattern:** containment, namings, mentions, orderings and blockage each walk the same five steps.\n  - Copy the before-map.\n  - Build arriving.\n  - Gather the keys the edit could have moved from arriving + outgoing.\n  - Per key, take the survivors (filtered by TOUCHED FILE, not by record) plus the arrivals in a promised order.\n  - Drop the key if it ends empty rather than storing an empty list.\n- **#237** added the third of those and designed the extraction rather than skipping it.\n- A generic `refiled<T>` needs the entry `Located` projected back out (the indexes hold different entry shapes), then has to hand back three things: the rewritten map, the keys that VANISHED, and whether a first-namer MOVED.\n- Only `namings` asks for the last two, because only `namedBy` promises key order — two axes behind one contract, with the caller paying for neither unless needed.\n- **Rule invoked:** the repo's existing author rule — a shared fixture is the right move at four occurrences, not three — says the SIXTH index is what should force the extraction.\n- **Why this node exists:** so the sixth becomes the trigger, rather than becoming the sixth silent copy.\n- **Status:** the invariants are re-argued per index today; `patch.test.ts`'s oracle is the only thing holding the copies in step.","created":"2026-08-18T06:05:00-04:00","changed":"2026-08-20T20:28:46-04:00","custom":{"from":"237"}}
{"id":"follow-one-unit","parent":"def-infra","ord":"a3","title":"Fold Link and Tree.tsx into useFollow #techdebt #deferral","done":"2026-08-20T20:32:37-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-20 at #284's merge from its Deferrals (the dag gate: a thing left \"for the human\" becomes a roadmap node).\n- #284 gave router.tsx a `useFollow` — the one tail (`followedSplit` → `openRight`, else `followed` → `go`) — called by PageView's delegated listener and the chat transcript's. Its altitude pass argued that `Link` and `Tree.tsx:396` carry the same two halves (route-off-the-event + open-it) and could be rewired onto it, deleting two exported functions and making the \"one spelling\" claim structural rather than documentary.\n- Not taken there because it is `Link` — every navigation in the app — changed for zero behaviour on a bug-fix PR whose node said do not widen scope. What WAS taken: the two now spell the force bit identically and the Link docstring no longer overclaims.\n- A behaviour-preserving refactor with the whole navigation e2e surface as its net; worth its own small PR when someone is next in router.tsx.","created":"2026-08-20T11:29:01-04:00","changed":"2026-08-20T20:32:37-04:00","custom":{"from":"olai #284 deferral","retired":"2026-08-20 verification vs master 44bc6873, the human's ruling — the Tree.tsx half was never true (Tree.tsx:408 is a decline-guard, not a navigation; unchanged since #246), and #284's own comment at router.tsx:345-351 argues Link's exclusion is deliberate (route already in hand; reading it back off the href is a round trip through a string). The promised delete-two-exports payoff is impossible; closed rather than shrunk."}}
{"id":"names-table-once","parent":"def-infra","ord":"a4","title":"The names table is built twice per navigation #techdebt #deferral","todo":true,"desc":"Filed 2026-08-20 at #287's merge from its \"Seen, not touched\" (raised by the efficiency pass).\n- After #287 the names table lives in `names.ts` and holds by value, but `App.tsx` (for the chrome) and each pane (for its own rows) each build one over the focused pane's reading — the same scan twice per frame.\n- The fix is a field on `createReading` and a change to the readings register so the table is derived once beside the reading and read by both — not #287's shape (a `<For>` keying PR).\n- Retired or shrunk by the kolu upstream item (`reactivity-kolu-upstream`) if keyed reconcile lands first, since the per-frame re-derivation is what makes the double scan cost anything.","created":"2026-08-20T13:07:01-04:00","changed":"2026-08-20T20:32:37-04:00","custom":{"from":"olai #287 seen-not-touched","verified":"2026-08-20 vs 44bc6873 — the per-frame half is DISCHARGED by #299 (names.ts:39-46; measured in names.browsertest.ts:167-186: repeated frames and row-moves no longer reach the copy). What survives: both builds re-run per navigation/real rename (names.browsertest.ts:190-197) and a duplicate Map held beside the pane's. Re-scoped to the S tidiness fix: derive once beside the reading (PageView.tsx:74,77 + reading.tsx:294-308 register + App.tsx:248)."}}
{"id":"one-alert-row","parent":"def-infra","ord":"a5","title":"One markup for the refusal alert row #techdebt #deferral","todo":true,"desc":"The palette and the header box hand-roll the `role=\"alert\"` row the filter bar gets from `SaidLine` — one list, one sentence, three markups.\n\nFiled 2026-08-20 at #287's merge from its \"Seen, not touched\".\n- #287's `refusals.ts` unified the refusal SENTENCE across the filter bar, the palette and the header search box, and keyed their lines so a refusal is no longer re-announced per keystroke.\n- What is still three-fold is the MARKUP: the filter bar draws its row through `SaidLine`, the palette and the header box hand-roll theirs. Unifying it is a change to what three surfaces draw — its own small PR, with the live-region behaviour (one announcement per new refusal) pinned.","created":"2026-08-20T13:07:05-04:00","changed":"2026-08-20T20:28:46-04:00","custom":{"from":"olai #287 seen-not-touched"}}
{"id":"shortlist-row-freshness","parent":"def-infra","ord":"a6","title":"Shortlist rows carry their own freshness #deferral","todo":true,"desc":"Filed 2026-08-20 from #294's deferrals (strong reason ruled: a design change to surfaces none of that PR's five items name). CORRECTED after grok's review note 3 — the first filing named the doors backwards.\n- #294 gated a stale Enter at the two doors the audit named: `Shortlist.tsx` and `completing.tsx`. Still UNGATED (findings this node absorbs): the composer, palette and header-search takes over the same primitive, and Hypertext's own rewrite-rescroll (#294's \"Seen, not touched\").\n- The deeper shape: rows carrying freshness through `search/Result.tsx` — which all four shortlist doors already draw — or a taker on `createSettled` that cannot be called past a question that has moved. Either fixes the whole class at once instead of per-door gates.\n- The made decision it would subsume: a stale Enter is claimed and spends nothing, silently (dimming was rejected as flicker in a campaign about flicker); a pointer press is never gated.","created":"2026-08-20T15:17:36-04:00","changed":"2026-08-20T20:28:46-04:00","custom":{"from":"olai #294 deferral"}}
{"id":"router-owns-spent-landing","parent":"def-infra","ord":"a7","title":"router.landed() — a landing is spent where it is minted #deferral","todo":true,"desc":"Filed 2026-08-20 from #294's deferrals (strong reason ruled: a design change, not a line — Hypertext still reads the slug to BUILD the frame's URL, so it cannot be a hard clear).\n- \"A landing is spent once\" lives in the face today; router.tsx states the contract and enforces nothing. A `router.landed(…)` marking a landing spent (still readable, no longer an act) would put the rule where the value is minted and hand the preview pane (#286's useLanding) the same guard.","created":"2026-08-20T15:17:40-04:00","changed":"2026-08-20T20:28:46-04:00","custom":{"from":"olai #294 deferral"}}
{"id":"team-multi-writer","parent":"def-infra","ord":"a8","title":"Team hosting: several writers, one branch #deferral #needs-brainstorm","desc":"Pre-ruled deferral at #301's dispatch (the human plans to host olai as a team notebook with coworkers invited). What #301 promises is only that the auto loop cannot corrupt: never forces, never retries, never auto-pulls — a refused verb stops the loop with git's words on screen. Multi-writer needs the real answers: fetch, a merge policy, whose-work-is-whose in the UI. Rebase-before-push belongs here too (#301 deliberately did not auto-rebase: ops' pending.ts rule — resolving a divergence stays a conversation in a terminal — and a conflicted mid-rebase is the state auto-commit must never enter; the human saw the reading and did not object). Grok's review agreed with the deferral.","created":"2026-08-20T19:59:12-04:00","changed":"2026-08-20T20:28:46-04:00","custom":{"from":"#301"}}
{"id":"filter-highlight-cross-piece","parent":"def-search","ord":"a0","title":"A phrase across rendered markdown lights neither piece #deferral","todo":true,"desc":"The surviving half of #240's filter-highlight deferral.\n\n- **Closed half:** a needle inside a code span or link lit nothing — closed by #254 (a848677d): the highlight walk now enters those subtrees while the tag SPLIT stays off (NO_TAGS_IN).\n- **What remains:** a phrase spanning two rendered pieces of a title (across a **bold**, across a code-span boundary) selects the row but lights neither piece, because HAST text nodes carry no source offsets.\n- The fix is offset-preserving rendering — a different change.\n- #254 added a `not.toContain` pin so a later change cannot half-light it silently; docs/search.md names this as the one remaining corner.","created":"2026-08-19T11:01:07-04:00","changed":"2026-08-20T20:28:46-04:00","custom":{"from":"#240, narrowed by #254"}}
{"id":"palette-count-cap","parent":"def-search","ord":"a1","title":"The palette and header search cap at 8 hits #deferral","todo":true,"desc":"Filed at #248's merge (the count-line honesty PR).\n\n- The filtered page's count line now tells all three truths, but the ⌘K palette and the header search box still cap at 8 drawn hits with no denominator — `SearchAnswer.total` is already on the wire and uncounted.\n- Different surface, denominator and hider than the page's count line; also noted in docs/brainstorming/filter-in-place.md.","created":"2026-08-19T11:01:09-04:00","changed":"2026-08-20T20:28:46-04:00","custom":{"from":"#248"}}
{"id":"preview-postload-growth","parent":"def-viewing","ord":"a1","title":"A previewed page that grows after loading never gets a taller frame #deferral","todo":true,"desc":"#206's deferral 5 — found by three refactor checks and confirmed by a verifier; predates #206, but running JavaScript is exactly what makes drawing late content common, so #206 makes it matter.\n- **Symptom:** a chart drawn from a fetch, a details element the reader opens, a late web font — the frame keeps its pre-growth height.\n- **Converged fix:** instead of rationing height reports per width, accept reports but REJECT THE ECHO — a report within a pixel or two of the frame's own current height is a vh-page feeding its container back; everything else is honest growth.\n- A behavior change wanting its own scenario.","created":"2026-08-16T13:46:29-04:00","changed":"2026-08-20T20:28:46-04:00","custom":{"from":"206"}}
{"id":"fm-authored-record","parent":"def-viewing","ord":"a2","title":"Frontmatter as an authored record #deferral #needs-brainstorm","desc":"#302 made frontmatter keys document *properties* (prop:/has:). The remaining half: reading them as the record's own fields — a date: that the day page/agenda/calendar draw (documents on the agenda), a done: that is a mark, edges. Refused in #302 with the two-answers-to-one-word argument: all three date surfaces are readings of Node/Dated, so a frontmatter date selected by date: but not drawn would split the grammar. An arc, not a line; also named in docs/brainstorming/first-class-documents.md, format/src/frontmatter.ts's header, docs/format.md, docs/search.md. Also refused there: tags: values do not become face tags (a tag is a sigil in prose; prop:tags today), and nested/block/anchor YAML stays unread (CustomValue is text or list-of-text).","created":"2026-08-20T19:53:41-04:00","changed":"2026-08-20T20:28:46-04:00","custom":{"from":"#302"}}
{"id":"doc-page-props","parent":"def-viewing","ord":"a3","title":"Where a document page draws its own properties #deferral #needs-brainstorm","desc":"#302 hides the --- block from the document page render; the properties it carries are reachable on every search row, via read_document, and in the editor — but the page itself draws them nowhere. Where and how (a drawer like a node's, a header line, nothing) is an undesigned question; documents.feature asserts every element of a document page against theme/scale.ts, so this is a real design pass, not a div. list_documents deliberately reports no props until this is ruled.","created":"2026-08-20T19:53:42-04:00","changed":"2026-08-20T20:28:46-04:00","custom":{"from":"#302"}}
{"id":"perf-patch-residue","parent":"def-performance","ord":"a0","title":"The patcher's residue: a flat record array, nine index clones #deferral","todo":true,"desc":"- `patch.ts:283` allocates `[...ordered.values()].flat()` — every record in the directory, per patch, both sides of the wire.\n- `patch.ts:257` `new Map(byFile)` is O(files).\n- `patch.bench.ts:419-443` names the nine clones the overlay did not absorb: children, status, after, blocked, byFile, mirrorsOf, edgesTo, namedBy, taggedBy.\n- `model-indices.md:136` ranks the clones #2 of what a keystroke costs a tab, right after the framework merge that surface-deltas-frame is deleting.","created":"2026-08-19T16:58:59-04:00","changed":"2026-08-20T20:32:37-04:00","custom":{"from":"olai #263 deferral (the patcher's flat-list allocation), quantified by the O(n) sweep audit","verified":"2026-08-20 vs 44bc6873, the human's scope ruling — M half only tonight: the flat [...ordered.values()].flat() (patch.ts:293, load-bearing via Derived.nodes) and new Map(byFile) churn (patch.ts:267). The clone list is now TEN (byDay joined at #278; bench patch.bench.ts:435-436), but the browser side of the claim is dead (fold deleted by the flip) and the ten clones need a delete-capable overlay the docs argue against — that L half stays deferred with these facts."}}
{"id":"perf-faces-broken-walk","parent":"def-performance","ord":"a1","title":"faces/broken walks every key per frame #deferral","todo":true,"desc":"Filed 2026-08-19 at #265's merge (rode #263 as deferral 3; #265 numbered it without touching it).\n- faces/broken walks every key per frame; measured +0.1 to +0.3ms of a ~4.5ms frame (spread stated where the numbers live, packages/web/README.md).\n- /simplify in #265 found the cheaper form for whoever picks it up (see the PR's refactor commits for the note).\n- Deliberately untouched by #265 — not one of its four items.","created":"2026-08-19T19:39:07-04:00","changed":"2026-08-20T20:32:37-04:00","custom":{"from":"olai #263 deferral 3, requantified by #265","verified":"2026-08-20 vs 44bc6873 — APPLIES verbatim (directory.ts:107-140 names this node in its own comment; faces has no equals, broken pays the same walk; facesOf still flatMaps per file). CAVEAT: the cited numbers' bench (outlines.bench.ts) was deleted by #279 and packages/web/README.md no longer carries them — evidence must be a run-count browsertest probe, not a bench. Cheaper form from #265 still exactly applicable: one merged walk producing both."}}
{"id":"e2e-underload-full-census","parent":"def-performance","ord":"a2","title":"e2e: run the full-suite flake census at scale #deferral","doing":true,"desc":"Run the full-suite flake census at scale — `underload.sh RUNS=20 BUSY=48` / `SUITES=5` — after the scratch-sharing change.\n\nFiled 2026-08-20 at #281's merge (opencode: verification work not yet run — a deferral, not a finding).\n- #281 ran underload.sh on the two converted files only (RUNS=3: 3 runs, 0 drops). The full-suite run at the census's own settings takes hours and the spawn saving was 16 of 502, so the lane did not pay for it.\n- Worth running once, unattended, to learn whether the port/lock failure class moved at all and to re-baseline the census after the ~150-scenario cut and the sharing change. Output is a number in the README's census paragraph, not a code change.","created":"2026-08-20T11:06:24-04:00","changed":"2026-08-20T20:28:46-04:00","custom":{"from":"olai #281 deferral"}}
{"id":"filter-ask-carries-revision","parent":"def-performance","ord":"a3","title":"A filtered page searches the whole vault per frame #needs-brainstorm #deferral","todo":true,"desc":"Filed 2026-08-20 at #290's merge (reactivity PR 4's first deferral; the dag gate).\n- Measured in #290 over a 90,000-node vault: one bulk gesture (a thirty-row tick-off, serial procedure writes a round trip apart) costs nine whole-vault `search.matching` calls, one per page frame. The audit's prescribed client-side coalescer was built both ways and measured 9 → 8, then deleted: `@olai/store` already collapses disk bursts behind its 75 ms settle, and the serial gesture's frames are a round trip apart, so no client window short enough to keep the filter's counts honest can reduce it.\n- The fix is on the other side of the wire — either the ask carries the page's revision so the server answers an unmoved set from what it already computed, or the narrowing moves to the server with the reading (the direction `filter/asking.ts`'s own header asks for). Wants a short design note before a PR: which of the two, what the wire member looks like, what the reconnect re-ask (one extra match today, #290's fourth deferral) becomes under it.","see":["reactivity-kolu-upstream"],"created":"2026-08-20T14:01:11-04:00","changed":"2026-08-20T20:28:46-04:00","custom":{"from":"olai #290 deferral"}}
{"id":"changed-frame-tax-upstream","parent":"def-performance","ord":"a4","title":"changed()'s frame tax belongs upstream #deferral #kolu-upstream","desc":"Four kolu-side follow-ups from olai #299 (the reactivity finale), each named in that PR's body and ruled deferrable by its review: (1) registering on changed()/arrayKey drops kolu's tracker out of its O(1) path into a whole-frame framesEqual per frame — deliberate (it's what makes an equal reconnect snapshot silent), but the deleted frames.ts walked only the object spine above the arrays; the cheaper shape belongs upstream. (2) The keyed merge leaves the tracker holding a second full copy of every frame. (3) The schema walk in olai's per-member guard answers a question arrayKey poses for every kolu app — kolu's own guard checks neither the required/non-nullable rule nor the mixed case; it wants to live upstream. (4) The batched deltas delivery cannot honour a key, so outlines/heads/transcript gain nothing from declarations. Kolu-repo work — needs the human's ratification before anything is filed on kolu.","created":"2026-08-20T18:14:48-04:00","changed":"2026-08-20T20:28:46-04:00","custom":{"from":"#299"}}
